<b>Becoming a Reveller</b><br>
<p>What we're looking for in guild members are people who are a good match for the guild, both for us, and for you. To that end, we strive to be as open as possible about our goals and ideals, and equally as open about the things we don't want. </p>

<p>Here are a few issues to think about to see if you think you'll be a good fit. </p>

<p>
<ul>
<li>Do you want a guild to aid in your accumulation of items or wealth? </li>

<li>If you're farming an item from a low level mob that you don't receive experience from, and a group of younger players that does get experience arrives and wants to camp it, do you stay because you were there first?</li>

<li>Do you enjoy being creative with emotes and /say to entertain others and yourself?</li>

<li>Would you ever give away an item worth something just because someone else needed it and you didn't?</li>

<li>Is EverQuest about reaching level 50 (or 60 or 65) as quickly and painlessly as possible, or is it about enjoying the trip there, even if it's sometimes difficult? Is the path of least resistance always the most worthwhile?</li>

<li-Can one positive interaction with someone in EverQuest make a day of playing worthwhile, even if you didn't gain any experience or items?</li>
</ul>
</p>

<p>If you've read the charter and see what we're about, then you probably know what the answers are to these questions for those of us in The Revellers. If you feel like you share our major beliefs and goals, and would like to join us, please fill out the application below.</p>
